WEBVTT

00:01.900 --> 00:05.730
<i>This world is filled with 
too many games to count,</i>

00:06.980 --> 00:11.240
<i>though the vast majority simply 
come and go in obscurity.</i>

00:12.580 --> 00:15.380
<i>The greatest of all games</i>

00:15.380 --> 00:20.720
<i>is the fully immersive VR game boasting 
over 30 million players worldwide—</i>

00:20.720 --> 00:25.320
<i></i>Shangri-La Frontier<i>, which rightly 
earns the title of "god-tier game"!</i>

00:27.000 --> 00:30.920
<i>One lover of trash games, Rakuro Hizutome,</i>

00:30.920 --> 00:34.130
<i>is trying out the god-tier 
game, </i>Shangri-La Frontier<i>!</i>

00:34.930 --> 00:39.620
<i>What adventures await him there?</i>

02:11.310 --> 02:16.360
<b>The Walking Air Purifier</b>

02:12.370 --> 02:13.490
Raising?

02:14.540 --> 02:15.610
Growth?

02:16.360 --> 02:17.850
That's it!

02:17.850 --> 02:20.220
I just need to do some raising!

02:21.070 --> 02:23.210
If there's no Ancient Craftsman around,

02:23.210 --> 02:25.950
I just need to turn Bilac 
into an Ancient Craftsman!

02:26.230 --> 02:28.670
Me, an Ancient Craftsman?

02:30.540 --> 02:32.590
You got it, bird-man.

02:33.180 --> 02:34.890
I'll play along.

02:35.250 --> 02:37.550
I'm gonna become an Ancient Craftsman!

02:37.550 --> 02:40.300
Yay, Big Sis Bee!

02:40.300 --> 02:41.880
Hell yeah!

02:41.880 --> 02:44.970
Let's start the plan to cultivate Bilac!

02:44.970 --> 02:46.400
Yes, indeed!

02:46.400 --> 02:48.810
Y-Yeah!

02:50.670 --> 02:51.560
So...

02:52.010 --> 02:55.570
What exactly is the plan 
to cultivate Big Sis Bee?

02:55.570 --> 02:57.330
Huh? No clue.

02:57.330 --> 02:58.440
Dumbass.

02:58.730 --> 03:00.320
Well, what do you expect?

03:00.550 --> 03:01.810
Listen up.

03:01.810 --> 03:05.740
To be an Ancient Craftsman, 
you gotta get two things.

03:01.950 --> 03:05.740
<b>Ancient Craftsman</b>

03:06.150 --> 03:07.490
And what are those?

03:08.040 --> 03:12.230
The first is a remnant from 
the Divinity, a Legacy Weapon.

03:11.140 --> 03:16.250
<b>Legacy Weapon</b>

03:12.230 --> 03:16.250
A weapons craftsman can't forge crap 
with just speculation and theory.

03:17.800 --> 03:20.510
And the other, according to Pops...

03:21.540 --> 03:27.010
is a marjik oppleration zoonit.

03:27.750 --> 03:31.270
A "marjik oppleration zoonit"?

03:34.710 --> 03:37.900
Are you trying to say 
"magic operations unit"?

03:36.540 --> 03:37.900
<b>Magic Operations Unit</b>

03:40.580 --> 03:43.200
Yeah, maybe that's one way to say it.

03:43.200 --> 03:44.920
Pretty sure that's the only way to say it!

03:46.820 --> 03:48.450
Point is!

03:48.770 --> 03:52.700
If I'm gonna be an Ancient Craftsman, 
I gotta have a working Legacy Weapon

03:52.700 --> 03:55.670
and a marjik oppleration zoonit!

03:55.670 --> 03:56.850
Get it?!

03:56.850 --> 04:00.960
Neither is gonna be easy to find!

04:02.580 --> 04:04.940
A Legacy Weapon, huh?

04:04.940 --> 04:07.180
That'd be a weapon from 
the Divinity era, right?

04:07.600 --> 04:09.170
Sunraku-san?

04:09.550 --> 04:11.170
'Scuse me a minute.

04:16.370 --> 04:17.690
Sunraku-san?!

04:17.960 --> 04:19.820
Where'd that guy get off to?

04:25.330 --> 04:26.850
Here we go.

04:28.390 --> 04:31.180
A "Legacy Weapon" would be 
something like this, right?

04:34.380 --> 04:39.040
H-How'd you get your hands on this thing?!

04:39.450 --> 04:42.160
Just a little something I 
got for beating Wethermon.

04:43.220 --> 04:45.970
<b>Non-Standard Armament: Blade 
Harbinger</b>

04:44.720 --> 04:48.330
That's a Legacy Weapon, all right...

04:49.040 --> 04:52.120
But you need a working one, right?

04:52.120 --> 04:55.020
I'm betting it won't gain "working" status

04:55.530 --> 05:00.610
until I fix this Ether Reactor thing.

05:00.990 --> 05:05.820
The reason I need a working Legacy Weapon 
to make myself an Ancient Craftsman,

05:06.860 --> 05:09.520
is so I can learn techniques 
from the Divinity.

05:11.810 --> 05:15.870
I just need something in good enough 
shape for me to figure out how it works.

05:17.250 --> 05:19.880
One in this good o' shape 
oughta do me just fine!

05:19.880 --> 05:21.930
Oh, great!

05:24.600 --> 05:26.630
Okay, then...

05:26.930 --> 05:29.160
Time to strip it down!

05:29.160 --> 05:30.510
Hey, wait a second!

05:30.750 --> 05:34.290
What now? I'm all ready to go, here!

05:34.290 --> 05:35.820
Sorry...

05:35.820 --> 05:39.630
I can't let you break it down without 
consent from a few other people.

05:39.630 --> 05:40.520
Yeah?

05:41.290 --> 05:47.490
<i>Yeah... this Legacy Weapon 
came from the Inventoria.</i>

05:47.950 --> 05:54.210
<i>Katzo and Pencilgon made it sound like the 
weapons and armaments in the Inventoria</i>

05:53.290 --> 05:56.290
Non-Standard Armament: Wire
Keep-Out Wire

05:53.290 --> 05:56.290
Non-Standard Armament: Blade 
Harbinger

05:54.210 --> 05:57.460
are shared between the three of us.

05:58.120 --> 06:02.290
Which means we all share possession of it.

06:02.290 --> 06:03.890
Fine.

06:04.480 --> 06:09.040
Then I guess you better find the other thing 
I need, the marjik oppleration zoonit.

06:09.370 --> 06:11.050
Let's see...

06:11.050 --> 06:15.460
Pops says you can find one 
in the Ruins of Past Glories.

06:15.460 --> 06:18.350
Hey, that's a pretty detailed map!

06:18.630 --> 06:19.850
Lemme see!

06:19.850 --> 06:20.740
Hey.

06:21.510 --> 06:26.150
Okay... I'm departing out of Thirdrema, so...

06:25.400 --> 06:30.660
<b>Prismatic Forest Grotto</b>

06:26.150 --> 06:31.890
I'll pass through the Prismatic Forest 
Grotto to the fourth city, Fourfolkshire.

06:30.680 --> 06:33.160
<b>Fourfolkshire</b>

06:32.300 --> 06:37.370
Then I'll pass through the Canyon of Ancient 
Souls to the eighth city, Eighthold.

06:33.180 --> 06:36.290
<b>Canyon of Ancient Souls</b>

06:36.310 --> 06:38.640
<b>Eighthold</b>

06:37.370 --> 06:42.040
From there, halfway to 
the 11th city, Eleventar,

06:40.310 --> 06:46.340
<b>Eleventar</b>

06:42.040 --> 06:45.750
is our destination, 
the Ruins of Past Glories.

06:43.440 --> 06:46.340
<b>Ruins of Past Glories</b>

06:46.340 --> 06:50.120
Looks like there's a lot of 
path splits after Thirdrema.

06:50.120 --> 06:55.060
It'll be a pretty straightforward 
route, but it'll be a long way.

06:56.310 --> 07:01.190
<b>The Lightless Barrens</b>

06:56.900 --> 06:58.740
Wait, just past Eleventar...

06:59.220 --> 07:01.190
The Lightless Barrens?!

07:01.310 --> 07:10.310
<b></b>Bonus Unique Scenario
<b>Vorpal Epic
</b>Items Needed
Receiver Delta
 Positioner Delta
 Transmitter Delta

07:01.560 --> 07:04.580
Let's see... Items needed...

07:04.580 --> 07:10.320
Receiver Delta, Positioner Delta, 
Transmitter Delta...

07:10.930 --> 07:14.810
I think I get the gist, but where do 
I even start looking for these things?

07:14.810 --> 07:17.660
Surely you're not going 
to send me out blind...

07:17.980 --> 07:18.880
Right.

07:19.400 --> 07:23.170
Check out a place called 
the Lightless Barrens.

07:23.770 --> 07:25.610
That's the place Aniki Vash said

07:25.610 --> 07:29.670
would have the items I need 
for my bonus unique scenario!

07:30.120 --> 07:32.730
Is this fate conspiring 
to send me right to it?!

07:32.730 --> 07:34.090
Hell yeah!

07:34.090 --> 07:36.650
I'm super hype for this now!

07:36.650 --> 07:39.220
Let's get moving!

07:39.220 --> 07:40.680
Hang on a sec.

07:40.680 --> 07:42.620
I gotta pack for the trip.

07:44.500 --> 07:48.110
Oh, cool! Bilac's coming, too?

07:48.110 --> 07:50.090
Though that does raise the question...

07:50.090 --> 07:54.110
How do I get out of the city, 
carting two rabbits around?

07:54.510 --> 07:57.580
I can sort of hide Emul by wearing 
her around my neck, but...

07:58.190 --> 08:02.460
Maybe Bilac's gonna have to chug MP 
recovery items to maintain a human form?

08:02.460 --> 08:04.650
Oh, I can't transform into a human.

08:04.650 --> 08:06.960
What, really? What do we do, then?

08:06.960 --> 08:10.340
Well, I can't become a human, but...

08:19.940 --> 08:21.890
Let's do this, Emul!

08:21.890 --> 08:23.520
Righty-o!

08:24.770 --> 08:27.690
Behold our powers of camouflage!

08:27.690 --> 08:29.020
Yes, indeed!

08:37.020 --> 08:39.230
You got yourself a perfect fur coat...

08:39.230 --> 08:41.330
...and fashionable scarf.

08:42.520 --> 08:43.930
Okay, whatever.

08:43.930 --> 08:48.230
Okay! Let's head through Fourfolkshire 
and on to the Canyon of Ancient Souls!

08:48.230 --> 08:49.930
Get moving, bird-man!

08:49.930 --> 08:51.780
Could you at least learn my name?

08:51.780 --> 08:53.720
Yes, let us away!

08:54.120 --> 08:56.050
First, though...

08:59.220 --> 09:04.690
Gotta set my respawn point 
in the Palace of Rabituza...

09:04.690 --> 09:07.440
<i>Respawn point registered.</i>

09:04.870 --> 09:07.440
Respawn point registered

09:07.440 --> 09:09.880
<b>Prismatic Forest Grotto</b>

09:08.140 --> 09:10.280
Okay, let's move!

09:12.170 --> 09:17.450
<b></b>Fourfolkshire

09:18.910 --> 09:21.030
<i>The Canyon of Ancient Souls.</i>

09:21.440 --> 09:24.240
<i>The site of the last battle 
in a war that occurred</i>

09:24.240 --> 09:28.120
<i>before humanity was as advanced as it is now.</i>

09:28.960 --> 09:35.230
<i>Ironically, the fighting had to be called 
off due to the arrival of monsters,</i>

09:35.960 --> 09:40.250
<i>but the large number of dead it produced 
caused miasma to cover the land,</i>

09:40.560 --> 09:44.410
<i>turning it into a nesting ground for 
undead creatures who despise the living.</i>

09:44.980 --> 09:49.050
Even now, it remains a 
grave danger to pioneers,

09:49.050 --> 09:52.270
infested with undead and 
curses... so they say.

09:52.270 --> 09:54.090
Don't tell me what they say!

09:54.570 --> 09:57.780
I told you to keep talk 
to a bare minimum in town.

10:09.290 --> 10:14.300
<b>Fourth City
Fourfolkshire</b>

10:14.300 --> 10:16.550
<b>Item Shop</b>

10:16.810 --> 10:23.560
You'll be in it deep, without a cleric 
or holy items to fend off that miasma.

10:23.560 --> 10:25.560
Yeah, I know.

10:25.560 --> 10:30.060
If you spend too much time in miasma 
you end up with "Hexed" status, right?

10:27.540 --> 10:30.060
<b></b>Hexed
Reduces max HP and stats by a certain percentage

10:30.060 --> 10:32.820
That's why we ducked into this item shop.

10:33.200 --> 10:36.100
I'm gonna get the items I 
need, then blow this town.

10:39.460 --> 10:40.750
Holy Water's pricey!

10:43.480 --> 10:44.550
Although...

10:44.550 --> 10:48.810
I might only need to buy anti-miasma 
stuff for you two guys.

10:50.670 --> 10:53.420
<b></b>Fourfolkshire

10:57.340 --> 11:00.680
<b>Canyon of Ancient Souls</b>

11:04.810 --> 11:09.270
Okay, got it. So this is the 
Canyon of Ancient Souls...

11:13.990 --> 11:15.770
Just like you described it...

11:16.130 --> 11:18.490
The air quality looks awful.

11:29.520 --> 11:32.000
<b>Canyon of Ancient Souls</b>

11:39.850 --> 11:41.050
Hang on a sec.

11:41.390 --> 11:44.010
How'd you get that aura 
of clean air around you?

11:45.740 --> 11:47.240
Noticed, did you?

11:47.240 --> 11:50.270
It's the effect of the 
mark Lycagon put on me!

11:51.380 --> 11:56.510
Any spell or curse from a source weaker 
than that dog gets canceled out!

11:56.510 --> 11:58.650
It can even nullify miasma?!

11:59.370 --> 12:00.310
That said...

12:00.770 --> 12:01.840
That said...?

12:13.810 --> 12:15.630
<b>Wyvern Zombie</b>

12:15.630 --> 12:18.440
Sunraku-san! It's a Wyvern Zombie!

12:18.440 --> 12:20.380
Dang, looks stinky.

12:36.340 --> 12:39.590
D-Did that happen because of the mark, too?

12:39.590 --> 12:40.660
Yep.

12:40.660 --> 12:43.780
Anything lower level than me just runs away.

12:44.340 --> 12:48.660
Too bad. I've got plenty of new 
skills I'd love to test out...

13:00.580 --> 13:01.950
Hey, Emul.

13:02.300 --> 13:05.650
I think that major level-up 
Wethermon handed me

13:05.650 --> 13:08.840
might have left me a tad overpowered.

13:08.840 --> 13:10.430
It does appear that way!

13:10.720 --> 13:14.750
"Keep your hands off the 
Night Emperor's prey," huh?

13:14.750 --> 13:17.560
They're a buncha cowards, if you ask me.

13:18.140 --> 13:22.390
Those Wyvern Zombies are so damn scared, 
they even forgot they could fly.

13:22.390 --> 13:25.670
Guess this might just be a 
short stroll to the area boss.

13:25.670 --> 13:27.820
Impressive as ever, Sunraku-san!

13:28.030 --> 13:30.080
Still, it's kinda too bad.

13:30.080 --> 13:33.080
I was hoping for a chance 
to flex my skills, here.

13:33.080 --> 13:36.990
Y'know, I forgot to check 
out your stats, Bilac.

13:36.990 --> 13:38.580
Are you even any good in a fight?

13:38.580 --> 13:40.100
What'd you say?!

13:40.100 --> 13:42.250
You saying I'm no good? Huh?!

13:42.250 --> 13:44.790
I was kidding, I swear.

13:53.670 --> 13:56.250
It didn't run from Sunraku-san on sight!

13:56.250 --> 13:57.690
It must be a powerful foe!

13:57.940 --> 13:59.890
That could be the case...

13:59.890 --> 14:01.690
Or maybe he just can't see me.

14:02.520 --> 14:05.070
He's got no head, see?

14:08.800 --> 14:12.410
<b>Rare Enemy
Dullahan General</b>

14:12.650 --> 14:15.200
H-He's letting us attack first!

14:15.200 --> 14:17.440
Maybe we can talk things out with the guy!

14:17.440 --> 14:20.380
Yeah, right! A dullahan 
don't even got a mouth!

14:21.090 --> 14:22.890
Yeah, fair point.

14:26.650 --> 14:28.300
He's readied his sword!

14:28.300 --> 14:29.990
Okay...

14:29.990 --> 14:31.800
Let's hunt a dullahan!

14:33.700 --> 14:35.310
<b>Empire Bee Twinblades
</b>equipped.

14:35.540 --> 14:37.100
Sounds good to me.

14:40.250 --> 14:42.310
Time to show off what I got!

14:42.310 --> 14:45.080
Yeah! Looking forward to it, Bilac!

14:45.080 --> 14:46.740
Yeah, Big Sis Bee!

14:46.740 --> 14:48.320
I'm greatly looking forward to it!

14:48.320 --> 14:49.650
Mimicking me!

14:49.650 --> 14:51.740
Y-You just said what I 
was going to, that's all!

14:51.740 --> 14:53.580
Quit messing around. We've got incoming!

15:04.630 --> 15:05.620
Here it comes!

15:05.620 --> 15:07.010
Got it!

15:07.630 --> 15:08.840
Ignition!

15:09.510 --> 15:13.040
Time to try out my new skills!

15:13.040 --> 15:15.370
You better handle your own 
miasma countermeasures!

15:15.370 --> 15:17.020
No worries there!

15:24.010 --> 15:26.170
I-It isn't safe!

15:26.170 --> 15:27.820
Keep your ears tucked, Emul!

15:43.310 --> 15:46.340
If Lycagon's Mark didn't chase it off,

15:46.340 --> 15:49.340
it must be a powerful opponent 
with a higher level than me.

15:51.610 --> 15:55.190
But somehow, I don't feel threatened at all.

15:56.770 --> 16:01.760
Maybe it's because I already fought 
the ultimate mounted warrior.

16:02.800 --> 16:05.190
First, let's get you off that horse!

16:14.770 --> 16:16.910
Okay, now!

16:16.910 --> 16:18.720
Vorpal Blade Tech!

16:23.500 --> 16:27.750
Vorpal Blade Tech
[Moon's Reflection] V3

16:24.310 --> 16:25.810
Moon's Reflection!

16:25.810 --> 16:27.190
Version 3!

16:30.650 --> 16:32.500
Watch yourself, buddy!

16:32.500 --> 16:35.410
If you try to turn around 
when you're off-balance...

16:42.890 --> 16:45.640
A dead body's bound to be light.

16:45.640 --> 16:47.770
Bet I can send you flying...

16:48.330 --> 16:50.500
So get going, pal!

16:50.500 --> 16:52.900
Megaton Swing!

16:52.900 --> 16:56.030
Megaton Swing

16:58.640 --> 17:01.820
Hey, nice hang time!

17:01.820 --> 17:03.910
Impressive as ever, Big Sis Bee!

17:04.170 --> 17:06.530
Don't let her show you up, Emul!

17:06.530 --> 17:09.510
We need a follow-up! Get a spell ready!

17:09.510 --> 17:11.630
I'll have Add Spell ready to go!

17:11.630 --> 17:13.070
Moon Jumper...

17:13.340 --> 17:13.550
Moon Jumper

17:13.840 --> 17:14.800
Into...

17:15.400 --> 17:17.280
Six-Boat Leap!

17:17.280 --> 17:20.260
<b>Six-Boat Leap</b>

17:24.320 --> 17:26.490
You wanna handle it yourself, eh?

17:36.000 --> 17:38.730
Playing second fiddle to an NPC...

17:38.730 --> 17:41.070
Any trash gamer needs to know when to do it.

17:41.070 --> 17:42.490
Sounds good to me!

17:43.480 --> 17:44.990
It's been thirty seconds.

17:45.370 --> 17:47.870
Ignition oughta be warmed up by now.

17:48.710 --> 17:49.880
Time to turn on the gas!

17:50.680 --> 17:51.880
Ignition!

17:50.900 --> 17:52.880
<b>Ignition</b>

17:53.640 --> 17:56.890
And with my luck in the 
triple digits at last...

17:56.890 --> 17:59.890
I'll pull out my luck-based attack skill...

18:00.430 --> 18:02.510
Hand of Fortune!

18:03.240 --> 18:05.640
Hand of Fortune

18:08.140 --> 18:09.290
And then...

18:09.770 --> 18:11.860
I equip Emul to my arm!

18:13.290 --> 18:14.490
I call this...

18:14.490 --> 18:15.940
The Rabbit Gun!

18:14.590 --> 18:15.940
<b>Rabbit Gun</b>

18:15.940 --> 18:19.070
Th-This is hardly appropriate treatment!

18:19.070 --> 18:20.240
Fire, Emul!

18:20.490 --> 18:22.510
Magic Edge!

18:27.580 --> 18:28.580
Right on target!

18:29.410 --> 18:31.080
Pretty weird way to fight,

18:31.320 --> 18:33.090
but you put him right where I want him!

18:35.740 --> 18:37.280
Hold your horses there, buddy!

18:38.760 --> 18:41.390
I'm gonna return your master to ya.

18:51.860 --> 18:55.360
Gotcha!

18:57.580 --> 19:01.110
Titan Blast!

18:57.990 --> 19:01.110
Titan Blast

19:14.120 --> 19:17.290
Now that was a big boom!

19:17.290 --> 19:20.010
Big Sis Bee! You're so awesome!

19:25.050 --> 19:26.410
Heck yeah!

19:28.570 --> 19:30.730
Yeah, that's about right.

19:30.730 --> 19:33.730
<b>Dropped Item
Dullahan General's Decapitator</b>

19:34.510 --> 19:37.980
"Dullahan General's Decapitator," huh?

19:38.650 --> 19:40.020
Let's see...

19:39.510 --> 19:52.000
<b>Dullahan General's Decapitator</b>

19:40.020 --> 19:44.240
"Attacks to the head deal bonus damage."

19:44.240 --> 19:49.150
"A longsword that likely once held 
great power, now rusted badly.

19:49.150 --> 19:52.000
It can only cleave flesh 
through brute force alone."

19:52.530 --> 19:54.390
Aw, it's all rusty.

19:54.390 --> 19:56.250
The edge looks lousy, too.

19:56.720 --> 20:00.160
"The corpse which had already 
lost its memories, its pride,

20:00.160 --> 20:02.260
and its love, even lost its head."

20:02.510 --> 20:04.920
"This is why the remaining 
torso targets the heads

20:04.920 --> 20:08.770
of not just the living, but also the dead."

20:09.120 --> 20:13.000
An "If I can't have my head, 
neither can any of you" sort of deal?

20:13.000 --> 20:15.100
Misery really does love company, I guess...

20:16.570 --> 20:17.770
Guess I'll sell it off.

20:17.770 --> 20:19.650
Mind if I take a look at it?

20:19.650 --> 20:21.280
Oh, sure.

20:25.640 --> 20:28.450
This sword's still got some life in it.

20:28.450 --> 20:31.290
I'll restore it to its former glory later.

20:31.740 --> 20:35.680
Hey, right. You're a blacksmith and all.

20:35.680 --> 20:37.050
I forgot for a second there.

20:37.050 --> 20:39.550
Hey, what's that supposed to mean?!

20:39.550 --> 20:40.630
<b>Emul
 Bilac</b>

20:44.490 --> 20:47.010
<b>Bilac Lv: 98
 Master Craftsman Sub: Archaeologist
 Vorpal Bunny Master Smith
Skill Points Remaining: 0</b>

20:49.210 --> 20:51.810
Level... 98?

20:51.810 --> 20:53.250
Pretty strong...

20:53.970 --> 20:57.200
And right after I finally outlevel Emul...

20:57.200 --> 21:00.550
That's experience I earned from smithing.

21:00.550 --> 21:02.900
You've got more experience fighting, for sure.

21:03.590 --> 21:07.210
If you socked me in the face, 
you'd probably break my neck.

21:07.210 --> 21:10.410
Hey! Just what's that supposed to mean?!

21:10.700 --> 21:13.610
Silence is golden, as they say.

21:13.610 --> 21:15.160
As they say.

21:16.400 --> 21:17.670
Emul.

21:18.170 --> 21:20.560
You're starting to take after bird-man here.

21:22.190 --> 21:23.590
Okay, let's go!

21:23.590 --> 21:26.230
We gotta get to that boss, lickety-split!

21:32.680 --> 21:37.730
We'll need that magic operations unit to 
make you an Ancient Craftsman, right, Bilac?

21:38.230 --> 21:40.820
Though I gotta say, the map here

21:40.820 --> 21:43.990
seems way more simple than the 
other areas I've been to...

21:44.250 --> 21:47.990
Nevertheless, we need only to 
proceed in a straight line!

21:48.470 --> 21:51.530
Yeah, it's easy-peasy!

23:27.670 --> 23:31.480
<i>SLF</i> Theater!

23:27.670 --> 23:34.220
<b>SLF Mini</b>

23:30.760 --> 23:34.220
<i><b>I Reincarnated Into a Trash Game?!</b></i>

23:31.680 --> 23:33.690
Mini!

23:34.220 --> 25:16.320
<i><b>SLF Theater</b></i>

23:35.340 --> 23:36.560
Sunraku!

23:37.170 --> 23:38.350
Sunraku!

23:39.240 --> 23:40.660
Open your eyes!

23:46.910 --> 23:50.370
Sunraku, you have been 
reincarnated in another world.

23:50.850 --> 23:51.560
Um?

23:52.000 --> 23:53.910
The trash game world!

23:53.910 --> 23:54.510
Um?

23:54.510 --> 23:56.490
You must defeat the Demon King!

23:58.190 --> 24:02.250
Aren't you gonna move at all, Goddess?!

24:03.210 --> 24:08.750
<i>And thus, my brutal isekai 
reincarnation began.</i>

24:10.390 --> 24:12.880
<i>The enemies' levels were 
too high from the start.</i>

24:13.550 --> 24:15.390
What the hell? Huh? Huh?!

24:15.390 --> 24:17.340
I slipped halfway through the wall!

24:17.340 --> 24:20.020
<i>I was constantly getting trapped 
in the game's geometry.</i>

24:20.020 --> 24:22.950
<i>Sunraku, leave this to me! Go on ahead!</i>

24:22.950 --> 24:25.200
Go on ahe— ea— ea— ea—

24:25.200 --> 24:27.130
Okay, that's freaky!

24:27.130 --> 24:28.510
Your head, man! Your head!

24:29.070 --> 24:31.820
<i>My allies couldn't maintain 
a fully human form.</i>

24:32.670 --> 24:34.300
Wait. This is an isekai, right?

24:34.640 --> 24:35.520
Is it, really?

24:36.690 --> 24:41.680
<i>But I overcame all challenges and 
at last arrived at the Demon King!</i>

24:41.990 --> 24:43.040
Okay, dude!

24:43.040 --> 24:46.580
I've been through hell and back! 
I'm gonna murder your ass!

24:46.580 --> 24:51.110
Congratulations on making 
it this far, great hero!

24:56.430 --> 24:58.700
But I am the Demon—

24:59.680 --> 25:04.170
Lag isn't a game issue, 
it's a user connection issue!

25:05.990 --> 25:07.930
And that's when I woke up.

25:08.300 --> 25:11.460
Nothing like remembering how reality works
to wake you up from a dream, right?

25:12.410 --> 25:15.530
I don't even know what to say to all of that.
